# {ProjectName} — Web-Novel Writing Toolkit (Codex)

## Skill Routing Table

In the Codex CLI, prefer invoking via `$skill-name` or `/skills`; natural language can also trigger the corresponding skill.

| Command / intent | Skill | Description |
|------|-------|------|
| `$story-long-write`, write long-form | story-long-write | Long-form web-novel writing (chapter by chapter) |
| `$story-short-write`, write short-form | story-short-write | Short-form web-novel writing (emotion-driven) |
| `$story-long-analyze`, long-form teardown | story-long-analyze | Deep teardown of a long-form novel |
| `$story-short-analyze`, short-form teardown | story-short-analyze | Teardown analysis of a short-form novel |
| `$story-long-scan`, long-form market scan | story-long-scan | Long-form novel rankings and market trends |
| `$story-short-scan`, short-form market scan | story-short-scan | Short-form novel rankings and emotional windows |
| `$story-deslop`, de-AI-flavor | story-deslop | Removes AI writing traces |
| `$story-cover`, cover | story-cover | Generates cover images |
| `$story-review`, review | story-review | Multi-perspective adversarial review |
| `$story-import`, import | story-import | Reverse-imports an existing novel into the project structure |
| `$story`, web novels | story | Toolkit router · auto-routes ambiguous intent |
| `$story-setup`, prepare to write a book | story-setup | Environment deployment · one-click deployment of hooks/agents/AGENTS.md |
| `$browser-cdp` | browser-cdp | Browser CDP tool |

## File Structure

- `teardown-lib/` — teardown analysis output directory
- `{BookTitle}/prose/` — long-form novel prose chapters
- `{BookTitle}/prose.md` — short-form novel prose
- `{BookTitle}/setting/` — character settings, world settings
- `{BookTitle}/outline/` — volume outlines, chapter outlines
- `{BookTitle}/tracking/` — context.md, foreshadowing.md, timeline.md, character-state.md
- `{BookTitle}/benchmark/` — benchmark-book analysis

## Codex Project Conventions

- Codex custom agents are deployed to `.codex/agents/*.toml`; they become stable only after starting a new Codex session.
- Codex hooks are deployed to `.codex/hooks.json` and `.codex/hooks/`; the project `.codex/` layer must be trusted, and non-managed hooks additionally need review/trust in `/hooks` before they run.
- A matching outline must exist before prose is written: long-form `outline/outline_chapter_N*.md`, short-form `section-outline.md`. Codex hooks enforce this mechanically, but the skill flow itself must also honor it.
- After a compact, first read `{BookTitle}/tracking/context.md` to restore current writing progress.

## Collaboration Rules

Coordination between agents is defined by the responsibility boundaries in `.codex/agents/*.toml`; no separate coordination-rule file is needed.

## Restoring Context After Compact

Key writing context:
1. Current writing project name and progress
2. Recently discussed character-setting changes
3. List of unresolved foreshadowing
4. The current chapter's emotion/rhythm targets

If `{BookTitle}/tracking/context.md` exists, read it first after a compact to restore context.
